        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fcdf4703-58ef-5246-8583-dd4a0a432992",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leigh Silverman, Danielle Brooks, Jeanine Tesori, Brian Crawley, Doris Betts\n- Works: Violet, Chinglish, From Up Here, The Color Purple, Orange Is the New Black, The Ugliest Pilgrim\n- Awards: Tony Award, Drama Desk Award\n- Roles: stage director, actress\n\nFacts:\n- Leigh Silverman is an American stage director who has worked both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\n- Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and a libretto by Brian Crawley, based on Doris Betts's short story The Ugliest Pilgrim.\n- Leigh Silverman was nominated for the 2008 Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Director of a Play for From Up Here.\n- Chinglish is a comedy about an American businessman trying to launch a new enterprise in China, and it opened on Broadway in 2011 under the direction of Leigh Silverman.\n- Leigh Silverman was nominated for the 2014 Tony Award for Best Direction of a Musical for Violet.\n- Danielle Brooks is known for playing Tasha \"Taystee\" Jefferson on the Netflix series Orange Is the New Black.\n- Danielle Brooks received a Tony Award nomination for portraying Sofia in the 2015 Broadway production of The Color Purple.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "66a8967a-5b35-5eb1-9b56-c6297bab5577",
        "text": "Page: Leigh Silverman. Sentence: Leigh Silverman is an American director for the stage, both Off-Broadway and on Broadway.\nPage: Leigh Silverman. Sentence: She was nominated for the 2014 Tony Award, Best Direction of a Musical for the musical \"Violet\" and the 2008 Drama Desk Award, Outstanding Director of a Play for the play \"From Up Here\".\nPage: Violet (musical). Sentence: Violet is a musical with music by Jeanine Tesori and libretto by Brian Crawley based on the short story \"The Ugliest Pilgrim\" by Doris Betts.\nPage: Chinglish (play). Sentence: It is a comedy about an American businessman desperate to launch a new enterprise in China, which opened on Broadway in 2011 with direction by Leigh Silverman.\nPage: Danielle Brooks. Sentence: She is best known for her role as Tasha \"Taystee\" Jefferson on the Netflix original series \"Orange Is the New Black\", and for her Tony Award-nominated portrayal of Sofia in the 2015 Broadway production of \"The Color Purple\".",
